  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The two distinctive flavours in machboos are "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "loomi"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "loomi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " dried lime, approximated here with lemon zest and extra lime juice, and a few drops of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "rosewater"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "rosewater"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " stirred through the rice at the end. Both are subtle but the dish lacks its character without them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: cook the fish only briefly in the broth. Remove it before it overcooks, then return it to warm through on top of the rice for the final minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
